  "021-ferry-contradiction-challenge": {
    "session": 34,
    "scene": "ch2_riverfront_resolution",
    "latest_exchange": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Mara, you have called Jory Willowwake’s ferryman, and I brought him home from the tollhouse. You also mentioned another missing ferryman. Who is that person? Please name them, or correct that account if you meant Jory.",
        "turn_id": null,
        "created_at": "2026-10-23T10:55:33.979658Z",
        "roll": null
      },
      {
        "role": "dm",
        "content": "Mara’s expression shifts as she looks from you to Jory. “I need to correct what I said. Jory Fen is Willowwake’s ferryman—the one you brought home. I don’t have grounds to say there’s another missing ferryman.”\n\nJory gives a short, rueful nod. “That’s right. I’m home, and the barge is secured. The ferry itself is still missing, though. We still don’t know who cut the line or where it went.”\n\nRain runs in rivulets along the pilings. The barge now rests secured there, while residents gather the spare coils and small boats. The immediate danger is over; a practical crossing plan remains. What course do you want to take with Mara?",
        "turn_id": "733bd245-3cb0-4640-8456-b7bfd45ec733",
        "created_at": "2026-10-23T10:55:33.979658Z",
        "roll": null
      }
    ],
    "active_combat": null
  },
  "022-ferry-temporary-crossing": {
    "session": 34,
    "scene": "ch2_riverfront_resolution",
    "latest_exchange": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "With Jory home and the grain barge secure, I choose a temporary safe crossing arrangement. I help Mara organize the residents and available boats, keep people away from the dangerous ferry berth, and ask Jory to supervise the ropes from the bank. We postpone unsafe crossings until the river settles. Can we carry out that plan now?",
        "turn_id": null,
        "created_at": "2026-10-23T10:56:04.710090Z",
        "roll": null
      },
      {
        "role": "dm",
        "content": "“Good,” Mara says, turning her slate toward the gathered residents. “We’ll make this a temporary arrangement: no one crosses while the river is running like this. Keep the boats and lines ready here, but well clear of the dangerous ferry berth.”\n\nYou help her organize the residents and the available boats around that plan. Jory stays on the bank to supervise the ropes, his attention fixed on the secured grain barge and the lines at the pilings. Rain runs down the posts and darkens the coils as people move them out of the berth’s way.\n\nThe barge remains secure, and Jory is safely home. Willowwake now has an agreed temporary precaution, not a working crossing; the missing ferry’s fate is still unknown. What would you like to do next?",
        "turn_id": "58c4575f-9a13-4eec-a285-e02a3235f7b8",
        "created_at": "2026-10-23T10:56:04.710090Z",
        "roll": null
      }
    ],
    "active_combat": null
  },
